# Redis: Data Center Real-Time Operations
# Handles active alarms, technician queues, and live status dashboards.

# 1. Active Alarms (Pub/Sub & Set)
# When a sensor exceeds a threshold, an alarm is triggered.
# Publish event for dashboard listeners
PUBLISH alarms:site:us-east-1 "CRITICAL: Rack-055 Overheat (45C)"

# Store active alarms for new dashboard connections to fetch
SADD alarms:active "rack-055:temp_critical" "pdu-002:voltage_low"

# 2. Technician Dispatch Queue (List)
# Assigning tasks to the on-site team.
RPUSH dispatch:queue:us-east-1 "Task-101: Replace Fan Tray Rack-055"
RPUSH dispatch:queue:us-east-1 "Task-102: Inspect PDU-002 Breaker"

# Technician claims a task
LPOP dispatch:queue:us-east-1

# 3. Orbital Uplink Status (Key-Value with Expiry)
# Tracking if we have live connectivity to a satellite.
SET uplink:sat-101 "CONNECTED" EX 600
# If key expires, connectivity is lost (ground station pass ended).

# 4. Global Health Dashboard (Bitfield / Bitmap)
# Visualize status of 1000 racks in a hall efficiently.
# 0=OK, 1=Warning. Offset = Rack ID.
SETBIT rack:health:hall-1 55 1
SETBIT rack:health:hall-1 102 0

# Count how many racks are in warning state
BITCOUNT rack:health:hall-1

# 5. Geo-Spatial Index for Technician Routing
# Find nearest available technician to a failed cooling unit.
GEOADD technicians:location -77.48 39.04 "Tech-Alice" -77.49 39.05 "Tech-Bob"
GEORADIUS technicians:location -77.48 39.04 1 km WITHDIST
